WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.864
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.080
NARRATOR: Throughout
history, women have

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.790
enhanced their lips with color.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.650
Cleopatra led the way
over 2,000 years ago.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.340
She was crushed ants and
beetles to redden her lips.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.820
Today a tube of lipstick
does the job nicely--

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.845
no need to mess around
with crushed bugs.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.770
Lipstick comes in a case that
also serves as an applicator,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.810
and that's the beauty of it.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.690
Just twist the stick
and apply color to make

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.445
lackluster lips look luscious.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.600
Lipstick ingredients
include waxes,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.400
pigments, and moisturizers.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.640
A worker pre-weighs everything
following a formula.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.085
The exact blends are
usually a company secret.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.170
She pours the measured
ingredients into a kettle that

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.535
melts and mixes them together.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.430
She adds a plant-based
gel known as [INAUDIBLE]..

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:10.910
It will act as a skin softener,
and also enable the lipstick

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.035
to be smoothly applied.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:18.710
Different waxes-- carnauba,
candelilla, and beeswax--

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.720
add body to the mixture.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.630
The waxes will also give
the lipstick a certain sheen

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:24.710
upon application.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.450
With the base mixture
prepared, she now

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.460
whips up a batch
of pigment using

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.410
different iron oxide colorants.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.340
She scoops it onto
rollers that grind

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.130
the pigment particles while
rolling it into sheet form.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.500
It takes three passes
through the rollers

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:48.685
to fully grind the pigment.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:51.950
It's ready to be added
to the base mixture.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.360
She lowers the heat
in the kettle to avoid

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.830
scalding the ingredients.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.890
She adds pigment
until the mixture

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:02.615
thickens and becomes creamy.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.764
It's now the right consistency
to be shaped into lipstick.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:15.720
It's over to the
next station, where

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.700
another worker
pours the lipstick

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.250
liquid into a filling machine.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.740
This filling system
also has a mixer that

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:25.560
keeps the consistency creamy.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.930
She places a mold under
the filling machine

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.670
and activates a lift.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.940
It serves up the mold to nozzles
that pump lipstick liquid

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.380
into the slots of the mold.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.460
She continues to
fill lipstick molds

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.910
until the supply in the
machine has been depleted.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.460
She places the
molds on a conveyor,

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:45.960
which takes them
through a nearly

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.660
5-foot-long cooling tunnel.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:52.110
The chilly trip causes the
lipstick liquid to solidify.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.800
The lipsticks are
now ready for their

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.590
swiveling tubular containers.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:03.590
She places a rack
on top of the mold,

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.170
and inserts the cases
into slots in the rack.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.690
The slots are aligned with
the lipsticks in the mold.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.650
Then it's over to the
turnaround machine.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.600
Bursts of air gently push
the lipstick out of the mold

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.820
and up into the cases.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:25.490
To assist, little
pushers apply pressure

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.720
to the bottoms of the cases.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.060
The lipsticks have made their
transfer without a smudge.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.850
She sets them down and
removes the transfer rack.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.020
On another conveyor, the
lipsticks pass by heat guns.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.540
The hot air melts the
lipsticks just a little

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.530
to make them shine.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.610
Continuing on, the
lipsticks travel

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.310
pass rollers that turn
the cases to cause

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:52.960
the lipsticks to swivel down.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.120
A tester samples of
lipstick from every batch

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.100
to determine the melting point.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:01.870
This is important,
because lipsticks

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.530
should be stable enough not to
melt in a purse on a hot day.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:11.260
He smears lipstick
shavings onto a glass disk

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.170
and examines their consistency.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:19.820
He places the sample
on a heating element

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.660
and swings a magnifying glass
overhead for a close-up view

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.030
as the lipstick shavings
melt into a puddle.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:32.390
Checking the thermometer, he
confirms that the melting point

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.875
is within an acceptable range.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.160
Another worker then
compares the color

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.940
of the freshly made lipstick to
the standard, and it's a match.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.340
So they ramp up production
with a plastic cap.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.235
The cap is clear to showcase
the shade of the lipstick.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.820
It has taken about a day to
manufacture this lipstick.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.750
It's time to freshen up.

